commit bd12a553fd3a5a86e7b068656b0e8bcb07c54fce

C03: the catalog provider waits for the first window of a slow client; the inert launcher-policy change reverted (APPS1611)

APPS1609 measured that «Abre Steam» still failed verification at 3.6 s: the product wires WindowsInstalledApplicationOpenProvider for catalog applications, which already accepts steamwebhelper by process-name prefix, but its verification budget was 28 polls of 100 ms and Steam shows its login window 4.6 s after launch (its main window at 7.9 s). The budget is now 120 polls; the launch is verified the moment the window shows, so a prompt application pays nothing. NotepadIdentityPolicy returns to its content before APPS1609: that policy serves WindowsApplicationLauncher, which the product does not wire, and the change was measured inert.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


